== Usage ==
{{Main|Opacity/Placement}}Similarly to other types of [[Lantern (disambiguation)|lanterns]], lanterns can either be placed on top of, or hung from, the surfaces of most solid blocks (though some blocks will require {{control|sneaking}}).

To place a lantern on top of a block, aim at the block's top face, and press {{Control|use}}. To hang a lantern from the bottom of a block, aim at the block's bottom face, and press {{Control|use}}. Also similarly to other lanterns, if a lantern is hung from the bottom face of a [[chain]], the lantern and the chain will connect seamlessly.

Lanterns can also be placed by pressing {{Control|use}} on a block ''adjacent to'' an air block the lantern could occupy, much like other types of lantern. Pressing {{Control|use}} on the top half of the adjacent block will hang the lantern from the bottom of an above block, and pressing {{Control|use}} on the bottom half of the adjacent block will place the lantern down on the top face of a bottom block.

Like other types of lantern, if a lantern exists on an ''invalid'' surface (a surface where the soul lantern could not normally be placed on), the  lantern will break and drop itself, upon the invalid surface receiving a [[block update]].

=== Light ===
The lantern is among the [[Light#Light-emitting blocks|most luminous of light sources]], emitting a light level of 15. Lanterns also melt [[snow layer]]s within 2 blocks and [[ice]] within 3 blocks ([[taxicab distance]]).

When the [[Render Dragon Features for Creators]] experiment is enabled in ''[[Minecraft Preview]]'', the inside of lanterns emits colored [[Vibrant Visuals#Point lighting|point lighting]] with {{Color|#f39a5e}}. The casing of the lantern blocks a part of the light and casts some shadows around the lantern.

=== Piston interactivity ===
A lantern is destroyed when a [[piston]] tries to push it. It cannot be pulled by [[sticky piston]]s.

